                <pb facs="0449" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg377"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 22113/6.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Brown.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-11-06"><hi rendition="#italic">November 6,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In re the detention by Honduras of the Perlas Co.’s launch, Mr. Knox instructs
                    Mr. Brown to remind the minister for foreign affairs that the Government of the
                    United States has upon occasion asserted and exercised the right to restore to
                    the legitimate use of American owners vessels that had been impressed by
                    revolutionists, even going so far, in the Colombian revolution of 1885, as the
                    retaking by a warship of such a vessel on the seas. Mr. Knox expresses the hope,
                    however, that this aspect of the question will not be presented for
                    discussion.</p>
            </div>
